REAL BUG — CAUGHT BY THE OPERATOR TESTING LIVE, NOT BY A GUARDRAIL — 2026-08-05

Not a constructed example, and not a case where a deterministic script caught
this before it shipped — it didn't. `tools/accessibility-check.py` has no
check at all for "every animated scene component reads the paused/reduced-
motion prop." That's a real, currently-unfilled gap in this project's static
checks, being written down here rather than left implicit.

What happened: the Sparks/SmokeWisps/CharredPit components added earlier
this session for the Ash Warden's fire pit each run their own useFrame loop
keyed off clock.getElapsedTime(), but none of them accepted or checked a
paused prop — they kept animating regardless of the header's Pause
animations control or the reduced-motion preference. This is exactly the
failure mode `.claude/agents/accessibility-reviewer.md` and
`.github/agents/accessibility-reviewer.agent.md` both list explicitly
("check the effect is wired to reducedMotion/paused, not just present in
the UI") — but that subagent is opt-in and wasn't invoked before this code
shipped, so nothing caught it until the operator noticed live.

--- a/src/EncounterLab.Web/src/scene/EncounterScene.tsx
+++ b/src/EncounterLab.Web/src/scene/EncounterScene.tsx
@@
-function Sparks() {
+function Sparks({ paused }: { paused: boolean }) {
   ...
   useFrame(({ clock }) => {
+    if (paused) return;
     const attribute = pointsRef.current?.geometry.attributes.position...
@@
-function SmokeWisps() {
+function SmokeWisps({ paused }: { paused: boolean }) {
   ...
   useFrame(({ clock }) => {
+    if (paused) return;
     const time = clock.getElapsedTime();
@@
-function CharredPit() {
+function CharredPit({ paused }: { paused: boolean }) {
   ...
   useFrame(({ clock }) => {
-    if (!rim.current) return;
+    if (paused || !rim.current) return;
@@
-      <CharredPit />
-      <Sparks />
-      <SmokeWisps />
+      <CharredPit paused={paused} />
+      <Sparks paused={paused} />
+      <SmokeWisps paused={paused} />

`paused` here is the same prop EnemyModel already receives and BrivModel/
CombatEffect already use — the fix is only that these three new components
weren't wired into it, not that the source of truth was missing.

Re-run after the fix:

    $ python tools/architecture-check.py
    Targeted client-authority guardrail passed
    $ python tools/accessibility-check.py
    Accessibility static checks passed (WCAG 2.2 AA source guardrails).
    $ python tools/ui-quality-check.py
    Compact product UI checks passed.

Note what that second command does NOT prove: accessibility-check.py passing
does not mean this specific bug is now guarded against for the *next* new
scene effect someone adds — there is still no automated check for this class
of regression. See professionalize-governance-and-history or a future task
if that check is worth writing; it wasn't attempted here.
